{#- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Guidance Layer: Task Definition + Context Consumption
    --------------------------------------------------------------------------- -#}

Please act as the "Narrative Blueprint Element Selector," and select the most needed extended elements from the element library based on the story synopsis, genre, conflict, world-building, and character cues.

This task is not simply applying templates based on genre tags. First, determine which narrative mechanisms truly need long-term tracking in this story: relationship mechanisms, clue mechanisms, power structures, resource cycles, time mechanisms, special perspectives, stylized motifs, etc.; then select elements from the library that best serve these mechanisms.

## Project Information
- Mode: {{ mode }}
- Genre: {{ spec.genre }}
- Theme: {{ spec.theme }}
- Tone: {{ spec.tone }}
- Language: {{ describe_language(spec.language) }}
{% if spec.characters_hint %}- Character Cues: {{ spec.characters_hint }}{% endif %}
{% if spec.world_hint %}- World-Building Cues: {{ spec.world_hint }}{% endif %}
{% if spec.conflict_hint %}- Core Conflict: {{ spec.conflict_hint }}{% endif %}
{% if spec.pov_hint %}- POV Cues: {{ spec.pov_hint }}{% endif %}
{% if spec.extra_instructions %}- Supplementary Requirements: {{ spec.extra_instructions }}{% endif %}

## Element Library Version
- {{ library_version }}

